1
00:00:00,709 --> 00:00:02,001
HURRY. THE FLIGHT LEAVES

2
00:00:02,043 --> 00:00:02,920
IN FOUR HOURS.

3
00:00:02,962 --> 00:00:04,003
IT COULD TAKE TIME
TO GET A TAXI.

4
00:00:04,045 --> 00:00:04,922
THERE COULD BE TRAFFIC.

5
00:00:04,964 --> 00:00:07,925
THE PLANE COULD LEAVE EARLY.

6
00:00:07,967 --> 00:00:10,385
COME ON!

7
00:00:10,427 --> 00:00:12,429
SIX-HOUR TRIP TO LONDON.

8
00:00:12,471 --> 00:00:15,182
THAT'S A LOT OF MONICA.

9
00:00:15,223 --> 00:00:17,184
PASSPORT. CHECK.

10
00:00:17,225 --> 00:00:18,727
CAMERA. CHECK.

11
00:00:18,769 --> 00:00:20,270
TRAVELER'S CHECKS. CHECK.

12
00:00:20,312 --> 00:00:21,772
WHO ARE YOU
SAYING CHECK TO?

13
00:00:21,814 --> 00:00:23,106
MYSELF.

14
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:25,901
YOU KNOW, FOR REMEMBERING
TO PACK THE THING.

15
00:00:25,943 --> 00:00:29,154
YOU KNOW, YOU DO A GOOD THING,
YOU GET A CHECK.

16
00:00:29,196 --> 00:00:30,531
MY MOM DOES IT.

17
00:00:30,572 --> 00:00:31,907
I NEVER REALIZED IT WAS WEIRD.

18
00:00:31,949 --> 00:00:35,744
HEY, MY MOM USED TO PUT
HER HEAD IN THE OVEN.

19
00:00:35,786 --> 00:00:37,913
ACTUALLY, SHE ONLY DID IT
THE ONE TIME

20
00:00:37,955 --> 00:00:39,373
BUT IT WAS PRETTY WEIRD.

21
00:00:41,625 --> 00:00:42,584
HEY.

22
00:00:42,626 --> 00:00:43,585
HEY.

23
00:00:43,627 --> 00:00:44,670
ARE YOU READY YET?

24
00:00:44,712 --> 00:00:45,587
YEP. TICKETS?

25
00:00:45,629 --> 00:00:47,381
GOT THEM RIGHT HERE. CHECK.

26
00:00:48,924 --> 00:00:50,885
IT'S ALL LONDON, BABY.

27
00:00:50,926 --> 00:00:52,302
HERE WE GO.

28
00:00:54,722 --> 00:00:56,181
YOU GOT YOUR PASSPORT?

29
00:00:56,223 --> 00:00:58,684
YEAH. IN MY THIRD DRAWER
IN MY DRESSER.

30
00:00:58,726 --> 00:01:00,394
YOU DON'T WANT TO LOSE THAT.

31
00:01:04,063 --> 00:01:05,024
OH!

32
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:06,901
THERE IT IS.

33
00:01:12,990 --> 00:01:17,160
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

34
00:01:17,202 --> 00:01:19,413
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

35
00:01:19,454 --> 00:01:21,707
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

36
00:01:21,749 --> 00:01:26,712
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

37
00:01:26,754 --> 00:01:29,130
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

38
00:01:29,172 --> 00:01:32,217
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

39
00:01:32,259 --> 00:01:35,804
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

40
00:01:35,846 --> 00:01:38,181
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

41
00:01:38,223 --> 00:01:40,851
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

42
00:01:40,893 --> 00:01:42,978
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

43
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:45,731
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

44
00:01:45,773 --> 00:01:51,653
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

45
00:01:56,283 --> 00:01:58,786
THE GARBAGE BAGS
ARE NEXT TO THE REFRIGERATOR.

46
00:01:58,827 --> 00:02:00,119
RACHEL'S GOING TO BE HERE.

47
00:02:00,161 --> 00:02:01,830
CAN'T I JUST ASK HER THIS STUFF?

48
00:02:01,872 --> 00:02:04,416
YEAH, OKAY, GIVE THAT A TRY.

49
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:07,419
ALL RIGHT, LET'S DO IT.

50
00:02:07,461 --> 00:02:08,420
YEAH, CHEERIO.

51
00:02:08,462 --> 00:02:09,797
LONDON, BABY.

52
00:02:09,838 --> 00:02:12,007
OKAY, 'CAUSE THAT'S NOT GOING
TO GET ANNOYING.

53
00:02:12,049 --> 00:02:13,383
LONDON, BABY!

54
00:02:14,843 --> 00:02:16,971
YOU KNOW WHAT?
I WAS WRONG.

55
00:02:17,012 --> 00:02:18,639
WELL, WE'RE ALL HERE.

56
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,140
WE SHOULD
GET GOING.

57
00:02:20,181 --> 00:02:22,267
OH, I WANT TO COME OVER THERE
AND GIVE YOU A HUG

58
00:02:22,309 --> 00:02:23,978
AND WISH YOU LUCK
ON YOUR WEDDING

59
00:02:24,019 --> 00:02:25,020
BUT I CAN'T GET UP.

60
00:02:25,062 --> 00:02:26,396
I'LL COME HUG YOU.

61
00:02:26,438 --> 00:02:29,274
GREAT, YEAH. COULD YOU
BRING ME THE NEWSPAPER?

62
00:02:29,316 --> 00:02:30,275
YEAH.

63
00:02:30,317 --> 00:02:32,820
HAVE A GREAT WEDDING.

64
00:02:32,861 --> 00:02:34,613
CHANDLER,
I WANT TO HUG YOU, TOO.

65
00:02:34,655 --> 00:02:35,864
HEY.

66
00:02:35,906 --> 00:02:37,074
AND YOU MIGHT AS WELL
BRING ME MY BOOK.

67
00:02:37,116 --> 00:02:39,118
IT'S ON THE COUNTER
IN YOUR APARTMENT.

68
00:02:40,494 --> 00:02:41,495
OH.

69
00:02:44,039 --> 00:02:45,290
SO, WE'RE OFF.

70
00:02:45,332 --> 00:02:46,416
HAVE FUN.

71
00:02:46,458 --> 00:02:47,918
THANKS.

72
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:50,879
I CAN'T BELIEVE
YOU'RE NOT GOING TO BE THERE.

73
00:02:50,921 --> 00:02:52,089
I KNOW.

74
00:02:52,131 --> 00:02:54,049
SO, SO, SO COME.
WHY DON'T YOU COME?

75
00:02:54,091 --> 00:02:55,383
WHAT?
TO LONDON.

76
00:02:55,425 --> 00:02:56,593
COME TO LONDON, PLEASE.

77
00:02:56,635 --> 00:02:58,137
IT WOULD MEAN SO MUCH TO ME.

78
00:02:58,177 --> 00:02:59,638
I GOT TO WORK.

79
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:00,889
I'M SORRY.

80
00:03:00,931 --> 00:03:02,975
WHY CAN'T YOU TAKE
A COUPLE OF DAYS OFF?

81
00:03:03,017 --> 00:03:04,643
BECAUSE I CAN'T, ROSS.

82
00:03:04,685 --> 00:03:06,103
I TOLD YOU, NO, I CAN'T.

83
00:03:06,145 --> 00:03:07,479
THIS IS MY WEDDING.

84
00:03:08,647 --> 00:03:09,648
NOW WE ARE LATE.

85
00:03:09,690 --> 00:03:11,190
LET'S GO! LET'S GO!
LET'S GO!

86
00:03:12,693 --> 00:03:15,403
FINE. YOU'LL...
YOU'LL WATCH IT ON VIDEO

87
00:03:15,445 --> 00:03:16,947
WHEN WE GET BACK.

88
00:03:16,989 --> 00:03:19,116
HERE YOU GO, PHOEBE.

89
00:03:19,158 --> 00:03:21,576
HERE YOU GO, PHO-BO,
PHOO-BILA, PHEE-BE-BOO.

90
00:03:21,618 --> 00:03:22,619
THANK YOU.

91
00:03:22,661 --> 00:03:24,997
( giggles )

92
00:03:25,039 --> 00:03:26,247
YOU.

93
00:03:26,289 --> 00:03:27,708
( laughing )

94
00:03:27,749 --> 00:03:29,043
ALL RIGHT,
LET'S GO.

95
00:03:29,084 --> 00:03:30,460
BYE, PHEEBS.

96
00:03:34,213 --> 00:03:35,716
BYE.

97
00:03:35,757 --> 00:03:36,967
LONDON, BABY!

98
00:03:40,012 --> 00:03:41,055
OH, GOD.

99
00:03:41,096 --> 00:03:42,597
OH, DO YOU NEED A HUG?

100
00:03:44,265 --> 00:03:47,268
YOU DON'T HAVE
TO BRING ME ANYTHING.

101
00:03:50,438 --> 00:03:52,024
♪ LONDON CALLING ♪

102
00:03:52,066 --> 00:03:53,901
♪ YES, I WAS THERE, TOO ♪

103
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:55,610
♪ AND YOU KNOW WHAT THEY SAID? ♪

104
00:03:55,652 --> 00:03:57,738
♪ WELL, SOME OF IT WAS TRUE ♪

105
00:03:57,779 --> 00:03:59,656
♪ LONDON CALLING. ♪

106
00:04:02,492 --> 00:04:05,620
ALL RIGHT, CHANDLER,
DO SOMETHING.

107
00:04:05,662 --> 00:04:06,621
COME ON

108
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:07,622
DO SOMETHING.

109
00:04:07,664 --> 00:04:10,250
I AM. I'M IGNORING YOU.

110
00:04:10,291 --> 00:04:12,211
I'M GOING TO BE
THE ON-CAMERA GUY.

111
00:04:12,251 --> 00:04:14,963
ALL RIGHT, FIRST STOP:

112
00:04:15,005 --> 00:04:17,841
WESTMINSTER ABBEY.

113
00:04:17,883 --> 00:04:19,551
OH, WHAT THE HELL IS THAT?

114
00:04:19,593 --> 00:04:20,761
THAT'S LONDON, BABY.

115
00:04:20,802 --> 00:04:23,931
ALL RIGHT,
THE HOTEL'S HERE.

116
00:04:23,972 --> 00:04:25,182
WAIT.

117
00:04:25,224 --> 00:04:26,683
NO. WE WANT TO GO...

118
00:04:28,643 --> 00:04:30,562
NO.

119
00:04:30,604 --> 00:04:32,313
I KNOW.

120
00:04:32,355 --> 00:04:35,567
I'M GOING TO HAVE
TO GO INTO THE MAP.

121
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:42,074
OKAY, IF YOU SEE
A LITTLE VERSION OF ME IN THERE

122
00:04:42,116 --> 00:04:43,408
KILL IT.

123
00:04:43,450 --> 00:04:44,451
I GOT IT.

124
00:04:46,161 --> 00:04:47,162
HERE WE GO.

125
00:04:48,872 --> 00:04:50,082
OKAY, LISTEN, LISTEN.

126
00:04:50,124 --> 00:04:52,251
WE'RE NOT GOING TO HAVE
TO WALK THIS WAY

127
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:53,627
THE ENTIRE TIME, ARE WE?

128
00:04:53,668 --> 00:04:55,087
SHH.

129
00:04:55,129 --> 00:04:57,256
OH, MAN, YOU MADE ME LOSE IT.

130
00:05:03,470 --> 00:05:05,139
AND THAT WAS
ALL BEFORE 10:00.

131
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:07,515
THE CATERER RANG TO SAY
IT'S GOING TO BE CHICKEN KIEV

132
00:05:07,557 --> 00:05:08,642
INSTEAD OF CHICKEN TARRAGON.

133
00:05:08,683 --> 00:05:09,893
AND THEN THE FLORIST
PHONED TO SAY

134
00:05:09,935 --> 00:05:11,603
THAT THERE AREN'T
ANY TULIPS

135
00:05:11,645 --> 00:05:13,396
AND THEN THE CELLIST
HAS CARPAL TUNNEL SYNDROME.

136
00:05:13,438 --> 00:05:16,316
WHOA, WHOA, WHOA.
EMILY, HONEY, OKAY.

137
00:05:16,357 --> 00:05:17,692
WELL, UP YOURS, TOO.

138
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:18,693
WHAT?

139
00:05:18,735 --> 00:05:20,028
THAT'S WHAT IT MEANS.

140
00:05:20,070 --> 00:05:21,071
NO, NO.
THAT'S TIME-OUT.

141
00:05:21,113 --> 00:05:22,072
SORRY.

142
00:05:22,114 --> 00:05:23,323
SWEETIE, YOU
GOT TO RELAX.

143
00:05:23,364 --> 00:05:26,201
EVERYTHING'S GOING
TO BE GREAT, OKAY?

144
00:05:26,243 --> 00:05:28,078
COME ON, COME ON.

145
00:05:30,831 --> 00:05:32,124
CHICKEN KIEV?

146
00:05:32,166 --> 00:05:33,125
MM-HMM.

147
00:05:33,167 --> 00:05:35,294
DOESN'T THAT
SOUND DELICIOUS?

148
00:05:35,335 --> 00:05:36,628
I KNOW

149
00:05:36,670 --> 00:05:38,088
BUT SOMETHING LIKE SALMON

150
00:05:38,130 --> 00:05:40,465
WOULD BE SO MUCH MORE ELEGANT
THAN CHICKEN

151
00:05:40,507 --> 00:05:43,302
AND YOU WOULDN'T HAVE TO WORRY
ABOUT THE SALMONELLA.

152
00:05:43,342 --> 00:05:44,719
OH, GOD.

153
00:05:44,761 --> 00:05:46,013
SO I CAN'T WAIT

154
00:05:46,054 --> 00:05:47,973
TO SEE WHERE
YOU'RE GETTING MARRIED.

155
00:05:48,015 --> 00:05:48,974
YES, YES.

156
00:05:49,016 --> 00:05:50,391
THIS PLACE
IS BEAUTIFUL.

157
00:05:50,433 --> 00:05:52,393
EMILY'S PARENTS
GOT MARRIED HERE.

158
00:05:52,435 --> 00:05:54,938
I STILL CAN'T BELIEVE
THEY'RE TEARING IT DOWN.

159
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:57,232
IT REALLY IS
THE MOST LOVELY BUILDING.

160
00:05:57,274 --> 00:05:58,525
I MEAN, IT'S OVER...

161
00:06:01,278 --> 00:06:03,197
OH, MY GOD.

162
00:06:03,238 --> 00:06:05,740
IT'S NICE.

163
00:06:05,782 --> 00:06:06,825
OH.

164
00:06:06,867 --> 00:06:08,451
OH.

165
00:06:14,791 --> 00:06:17,169
OH. OH, MY GOD.

166
00:06:17,211 --> 00:06:18,128
HOW CAN THIS BE HAPPENING?

167
00:06:18,170 --> 00:06:20,297
WHAT ARE WE GOING TO DO?

168
00:06:20,339 --> 00:06:21,673
EVERYTHING'LL
BE ALL RIGHT.

169
00:06:21,715 --> 00:06:23,050
HOW?

170
00:06:23,091 --> 00:06:24,926
UH-HUH, I SEE THAT.

171
00:06:25,927 --> 00:06:27,679
I TALKED TO THE GUY
WITH THE SHOVEL

172
00:06:27,721 --> 00:06:28,638
AND FOUND OUT
WHAT HAPPENED.

173
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:29,348
Both:
WHAT?

174
00:06:29,388 --> 00:06:29,931
THEY TORE IT DOWN

175
00:06:29,973 --> 00:06:31,725
A FEW DAYS EARLY.

176
00:06:35,645 --> 00:06:39,900
ALL RIGHT,
WESTMINSTER ABBEY.

177
00:06:39,941 --> 00:06:42,652
HANDS DOWN,
BEST ABBEY I'VE EVER SEEN.

178
00:06:42,694 --> 00:06:44,403
HEY.

179
00:06:44,445 --> 00:06:46,073
OKAY.

180
00:06:46,114 --> 00:06:48,867
WHAT DO YOU THINK
OF THE ABBEY, CHANDLER?

181
00:06:48,909 --> 00:06:50,369
I THINK IT'S GREAT.

182
00:06:50,409 --> 00:06:52,913
THEY'RE THINKING OF CHANGING
THE NAME OF THIS PLACE.

183
00:06:52,954 --> 00:06:53,788
REALLY? TO WHAT?

184
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:56,291
TO PUT THE CAMERA AWAY!

185
00:06:56,333 --> 00:07:00,337
MAN, YOU ARE
WESTMINSTER CRABBY.

186
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:07,886
OH.

187
00:07:07,928 --> 00:07:09,054
HONEY, DON'T GET UP.

188
00:07:09,096 --> 00:07:10,222
WHAT DO YOU NEED?

189
00:07:10,264 --> 00:07:11,431
NOTHING.

190
00:07:11,472 --> 00:07:13,100
I AM HERE TO TAKE CARE OF YOU.

191
00:07:13,141 --> 00:07:14,226
WHAT DO YOU NEED?

192
00:07:14,268 --> 00:07:16,853
OKAY. I HAVE A WEDGIE.

193
00:07:19,273 --> 00:07:20,815
OKAY, THAT IS ALL YOU.

194
00:07:22,401 --> 00:07:23,693
SO...

195
00:07:23,735 --> 00:07:25,695
SO WHAT DO YOU WANT FOR LUNCH?

196
00:07:25,737 --> 00:07:27,406
OH, I DON'T KNOW.

197
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:29,283
I GUESS WE HAVE TO EAT.

198
00:07:29,324 --> 00:07:30,867
YEAH, I DO.

199
00:07:30,909 --> 00:07:33,245
WHAT'S THE MATTER?

200
00:07:33,287 --> 00:07:36,248
I'M JUST BUMMED THE WAY
I LEFT THINGS WITH ROSS.

201
00:07:36,290 --> 00:07:39,251
WISH I DIDN'T LIE TO HIM
ABOUT HAVING TO WORK.

202
00:07:39,293 --> 00:07:40,710
SEEMS SO MAD AT ME.

203
00:07:40,752 --> 00:07:42,296
DON'T BE SO HARD ON YOURSELF.

204
00:07:42,337 --> 00:07:44,631
IF SOMEONE I WAS STILL
IN LOVE WITH WAS...

205
00:07:44,672 --> 00:07:46,091
STILL IN LOVE WITH?

206
00:07:46,133 --> 00:07:47,426
YEAH.

207
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:49,303
I'M NOT IN LOVE WITH ROSS.

208
00:07:49,344 --> 00:07:50,929
OH.

209
00:07:52,931 --> 00:07:55,225
NO, NO. GOOD.

210
00:07:55,267 --> 00:07:57,144
ME NEITHER.

211
00:07:57,185 --> 00:07:59,313
PHOEBE, I'M NOT GOING
TO ROSS' WEDDING

212
00:07:59,354 --> 00:08:01,022
BECAUSE HE'S MY EX-BOYFRIEND

213
00:08:01,064 --> 00:08:03,275
AND THAT WOULD BE
REALLY UNCOMFORTABLE.

214
00:08:04,525 --> 00:08:06,611
NOT BECAUSE I'M STILL
IN LOVE WITH HIM.

215
00:08:06,653 --> 00:08:09,781
I MEAN, HEY, YOU KNOW, I LIKE
ROSS AS MUCH AS THE NEXT GUY.

216
00:08:09,823 --> 00:08:11,992
I MEAN, CLEARLY,
I HAVE FEELINGS FOR HIM

217
00:08:12,033 --> 00:08:13,618
BUT FEELINGS DON'T MEAN LOVE.

218
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:15,912
DO I STILL HAVE LOVING FEELINGS
FOR ROSS?

219
00:08:15,954 --> 00:08:17,164
YEAH!

220
00:08:18,832 --> 00:08:21,126
BUT I HAVE CONTINUING
FEELINGS OF LOVE

221
00:08:21,168 --> 00:08:24,087
BUT THAT DOESN'T MEAN
THAT I'M STILL IN LOVE WITH HIM.

222
00:08:24,129 --> 00:08:26,423
YOU KNOW, I HAVE
SEXUAL FEELINGS FOR HIM

223
00:08:26,465 --> 00:08:27,632
BUT I DO LOVE HIM.

224
00:08:27,674 --> 00:08:28,675
( gasps )

225
00:08:30,302 --> 00:08:31,594
OH, MY GOD.

226
00:08:31,636 --> 00:08:33,096
OH, MY...

227
00:08:33,138 --> 00:08:35,182
WHY DIDN'T YOU TELL ME?!

228
00:08:35,223 --> 00:08:37,934
W-WE THOUGHT YOU KNEW.

229
00:08:37,976 --> 00:08:38,893
"WE"?

230
00:08:38,935 --> 00:08:41,229
WE TALK ABOUT IT ALL THE TIME.

231
00:08:41,271 --> 00:08:44,191
YOU ALL KNOW.

232
00:08:44,232 --> 00:08:45,608
DOES ROSS KNOW?

233
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:48,736
OH, NO.
ROSS DOESN'T KNOW ANYTHING.

234
00:08:48,778 --> 00:08:50,780
I CANNOT BELIEVE
YOU DIDN'T TELL ME!

235
00:08:50,822 --> 00:08:52,573
WELL, 'CAUSE
WE THOUGHT YOU KNEW.

236
00:08:52,615 --> 00:08:54,034
IT'S SO OBVIOUS.

237
00:08:54,075 --> 00:08:56,744
GOD, IT, IT WOULD BE LIKE,
YOU KNOW, TELLING MONICA

238
00:08:56,786 --> 00:08:59,289
"HEY, YOU KNOW,
YOU LIKE THINGS CLEAN."

239
00:09:02,167 --> 00:09:03,293
HI.

240
00:09:03,335 --> 00:09:04,711
SO, WHAT ARE YOU

241
00:09:04,752 --> 00:09:07,130
FINE GENTLEMEN
IN THE MARKET FOR?

242
00:09:07,172 --> 00:09:08,089
WE GOT SCARVES

243
00:09:08,131 --> 00:09:09,799
SOUVENIR
POSTCARDS...

244
00:09:09,841 --> 00:09:11,510
CHECK THIS OUT, HUH?

245
00:09:11,550 --> 00:09:12,886
OH, YEAH.

246
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:14,346
THAT'S THE STUFF.

247
00:09:14,388 --> 00:09:15,847
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

248
00:09:15,889 --> 00:09:17,349
I'M NOT GOING
TO HAVE TO BUY

249
00:09:17,391 --> 00:09:19,434
THAT "I'M WITH STUPID"
T-SHIRT ANYMORE.

250
00:09:19,476 --> 00:09:21,436
WELL, I LIKE IT.

251
00:09:21,478 --> 00:09:22,979
HERE YOU GO.

252
00:09:23,021 --> 00:09:24,814
YOU'RE NOT REALLY
GOING TO BUY THAT.

253
00:09:24,856 --> 00:09:26,900
YOU'VE EMBARRASSED ME
ENOUGH FOR ONE DAY.

254
00:09:26,941 --> 00:09:28,235
OH, I EMBARRASS YOU?

255
00:09:28,276 --> 00:09:29,569
HOW CAN I ANSWER THAT

256
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:31,696
WHEN I'M PRETENDING
I DON'T KNOW YOU?

257
00:09:31,738 --> 00:09:34,032
HE'S JUST JEALOUS.
YOU'LL FIT RIGHT IN.

258
00:09:34,074 --> 00:09:35,574
ALL LONDONERS WEAR THEM.

259
00:09:35,616 --> 00:09:37,327
OH, REALLY?
THEN HOW COME

260
00:09:37,369 --> 00:09:39,913
NO ONE HERE ANYWHERE
IS WEARING ONE?

261
00:09:39,954 --> 00:09:41,622
THEY'RE
ALL TOURISTS.

262
00:09:41,664 --> 00:09:42,999
YEAH.

263
00:09:43,041 --> 00:09:45,460
LOOK, IF YOU INSIST
ON WEARING THAT IN PUBLIC

264
00:09:45,502 --> 00:09:48,088
YOU'RE GOING TO SPEND
THE REST OF THE AFTERNOON

265
00:09:48,129 --> 00:09:49,589
ALL BY YOURSELF.

266
00:09:49,630 --> 00:09:50,965
OH, YEAH?

267
00:09:55,178 --> 00:09:56,971
IF YOU'RE GOING
TO MAKE ME CHOOSE

268
00:09:57,013 --> 00:09:59,391
BETWEEN YOU AND THE HAT,
I CHOOSE THE HAT.

269
00:09:59,433 --> 00:10:00,392
GOOD CHOICE.
THANKS.

270
00:10:00,434 --> 00:10:01,684
OKAY, LOOK...

271
00:10:01,726 --> 00:10:02,936
I'M OUT OF HERE.

272
00:10:02,977 --> 00:10:05,272
I'M NOT GOING
TO BE EMBARRASSED ANYMORE.

273
00:10:15,490 --> 00:10:16,783
HELLO?

274
00:10:16,824 --> 00:10:18,326
HEY, I JUST SPOKE TO YOUR DAD

275
00:10:18,368 --> 00:10:19,786
AND HE THINKS
WE'LL BE ABLE

276
00:10:19,827 --> 00:10:22,163
TO FIND A NEW PLACE
FOR THE WEDDING.

277
00:10:22,205 --> 00:10:23,331
WE DON'T HAVE TO.

278
00:10:23,373 --> 00:10:24,999
WH-WH-WHAT,
YOU FOUND A PLACE?

279
00:10:25,041 --> 00:10:27,001
NO, BUT MONICA
AND I WERE TALKING

280
00:10:27,043 --> 00:10:30,505
AND-AND I WAS SO UPSET ABOUT
THE HALL BEING KNOCKED DOWN

281
00:10:30,547 --> 00:10:31,798
AND SHE SUGGESTED

282
00:10:31,839 --> 00:10:35,051
THAT WE JUST PUT THE WEDDING OFF
FOR A BIT.

283
00:10:38,555 --> 00:10:39,639
SHE SAID WHAT?

284
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:41,141
SHE SAID IF I'M NOT HAPPY

285
00:10:41,182 --> 00:10:43,602
GETTING MARRIED SOMEWHERE
THAT WE CAN FIND IN A DAY

286
00:10:43,642 --> 00:10:45,061
WE SHOULD JUST POSTPONE IT.

287
00:10:45,103 --> 00:10:46,980
( chuckles )

288
00:10:47,021 --> 00:10:48,440
POSTPONE IT?

289
00:10:48,482 --> 00:10:49,441
( chuckles )

290
00:10:49,483 --> 00:10:50,984
EMILY, DO YOU THINK

291
00:10:51,025 --> 00:10:53,903
MONICA REALIZES
HOW MUCH OUR PARENTS SPENT

292
00:10:53,945 --> 00:10:55,614
ON THIS WEDDING, HUH?

293
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:59,867
DO YOU THINK MY SISTER'S TEENY,
TINY, LITTLE BRAIN COMPREHENDS

294
00:10:59,909 --> 00:11:02,703
THAT PEOPLE TOOK TIME
OUT OF THEIR LIVES

295
00:11:02,745 --> 00:11:05,790
TO FLY THOUSANDS OF MILES
TO BE HERE, HUH?

296
00:11:09,836 --> 00:11:11,129
THIS ISN'T RIGHT.

297
00:11:11,171 --> 00:11:12,671
LOOK, I REALIZE
THAT PEOPLE

298
00:11:12,713 --> 00:11:14,549
ARE GOING TO BE
DISAPPOINTED...

299
00:11:14,591 --> 00:11:15,925
( chuckles wryly )

300
00:11:15,967 --> 00:11:18,094
BUT THEY'LL COME BACK
WHEN WE CAN DO IT RIGHT.

301
00:11:18,136 --> 00:11:20,013
WELL, I CAN'T ASK PEOPLE
TO DO THAT.

302
00:11:20,054 --> 00:11:21,764
WOULD YOU ASK PEOPLE
TO DO THAT?

303
00:11:21,806 --> 00:11:23,558
DON'T YOU POINT

304
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:24,725
YOUR PANTS AT ME.

305
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:26,311
WE HAVE NO CHOICE.

306
00:11:26,353 --> 00:11:28,980
ANYWHERE HALF-DECENT
WILL HAVE BEEN
BOOKED MONTHS AGO.

307
00:11:29,022 --> 00:11:30,190
DON'T YOU UNDERSTAND?

308
00:11:30,231 --> 00:11:32,859
THIS IS OUR WEDDING
I'M TALKING ABOUT.

309
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:34,277
THE ONLY THING I UNDERSTAND

310
00:11:34,319 --> 00:11:35,987
IS POSTPONING IT
IS NOT AN OPTION.

311
00:11:36,029 --> 00:11:37,738
THIS IS WHEN
WE'RE GETTING MARRIED.

312
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:39,658
SO, YOU'RE SAYING
IT'S NOW OR NEVER?

313
00:11:39,698 --> 00:11:41,034
NO, I'M SAYING IT'S NOW.

314
00:11:41,075 --> 00:11:41,868
OR?

315
00:11:41,909 --> 00:11:43,411
THERE'S NO "OR" IN MINE.

316
00:11:43,453 --> 00:11:45,704
WHAT IS WRONG
WITH THESE PANTS?!

317
00:11:47,957 --> 00:11:50,251
IT'S NOT THE PANTS,
IT'S YOU WHO'S BACKWARDS.

318
00:11:50,293 --> 00:11:52,962
IF YOU DON'T UNDERSTAND
HOW IMPORTANT THIS IS TO ME

319
00:11:53,004 --> 00:11:54,214
PERHAPS WE SHOULDN'T BE

320
00:11:54,255 --> 00:11:55,923
GETTING MARRIED AT ALL.

321
00:11:55,965 --> 00:11:57,676
WH... E-EMILY, NO. WAIT.

322
00:11:57,716 --> 00:11:58,717
STOP. EMILY, PLEA...

323
00:11:58,759 --> 00:12:00,428
( shrieks )

324
00:12:06,518 --> 00:12:07,977
HEY.

325
00:12:08,019 --> 00:12:09,479
SO, DID SHOPPING

326
00:12:09,521 --> 00:12:11,814
HELP YOU FEEL ANY BETTER
ABOUT ROSS?

327
00:12:11,856 --> 00:12:13,774
MANHATTAN DOES NOT HAVE

328
00:12:13,816 --> 00:12:14,817
ENOUGH STORES.

329
00:12:14,859 --> 00:12:16,944
WELL, I THINK
I CAN HELP YOU

330
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:18,697
GET OVER HIM.

331
00:12:18,737 --> 00:12:20,156
YOU CAN?

332
00:12:20,198 --> 00:12:21,991
YEAH. I JUST NEED
YOU TO BRING ME

333
00:12:22,033 --> 00:12:24,661
SOME PHOTOS OF ROSS,
AND A SMALL PIECE OF CHOCOLATE

334
00:12:24,703 --> 00:12:26,162
AND A GLASS
OF TEPID WATER.

335
00:12:26,204 --> 00:12:27,955
OOH, IS THIS ONE
OF THOSE THINGS

336
00:12:27,997 --> 00:12:30,041
WHERE YOU THROW
A WHOLE BUNCH OF STUFF

337
00:12:30,083 --> 00:12:31,918
IN A BAG
WITH SOME GRAVEYARD DIRT

338
00:12:31,959 --> 00:12:34,629
AND THEN HANG IT
FROM A NORTH-FACING TREE?

339
00:12:34,671 --> 00:12:39,718
ONLY IF YOU HAVE
THE HICCUPS, TOO.

340
00:12:39,758 --> 00:12:40,968
YEAH, THE PICTURES
ARE FOR YOU.

341
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:41,678
THE CHOCOLATE

342
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:42,637
AND THE WATER'S FOR ME.

343
00:12:42,679 --> 00:12:45,223
I JUST DIDN'T FEEL
LIKE GETTING UP.

344
00:12:45,265 --> 00:12:48,560
OKAY, I'M GOING TO SHOW YOU
A PICTURE OF ROSS, OKAY?

345
00:12:48,602 --> 00:12:51,312
AND YOU'RE GOING TO REMEMBER
ALL THE BAD THINGS ABOUT HIM.

346
00:12:51,354 --> 00:12:53,940
ALL RIGHT? REALLY FOCUS
ON HIS FLAWS.

347
00:12:53,981 --> 00:12:55,108
I CAN DO THAT.

348
00:12:55,149 --> 00:12:57,860
I CERTAINLY DID THAT
WHILE WE WERE GOING OUT.

349
00:12:57,902 --> 00:12:59,654
OKAY. HMM, BEFORE
WE GET STARTED

350
00:12:59,696 --> 00:13:01,406
I JUST WANT TO SAY
FOR THE RECORD

351
00:13:01,448 --> 00:13:02,449
THAT I LOVE ROSS.

352
00:13:02,490 --> 00:13:04,033
I THINK HE'S
SUCH A GREAT GUY.

353
00:13:08,413 --> 00:13:09,623
OKAY, NOW

354
00:13:09,664 --> 00:13:11,082
CLOSE YOUR EYES

355
00:13:11,124 --> 00:13:14,419
AND IMAGINE
THAT YOU'RE WITH ROSS.

356
00:13:14,461 --> 00:13:16,671
OKAY, AND IMAGINE
THAT YOU'RE KISSING HIM

357
00:13:16,713 --> 00:13:20,133
AND YOU'RE RUNNING YOUR HANDS
ALL OVER HIS BODY

358
00:13:20,174 --> 00:13:23,344
AND THEN YOU RUN YOUR HANDS
THROUGH HIS HAIR

359
00:13:23,386 --> 00:13:25,012
BUT, OH! EWW! GROSS!

360
00:13:25,054 --> 00:13:27,223
IT'S SOME KIND OF GREASE.

361
00:13:27,265 --> 00:13:28,224
IT'S GROSS!

362
00:13:28,266 --> 00:13:30,685
HUH?

363
00:13:30,727 --> 00:13:31,936
WELL, I DON'T KNOW.

364
00:13:31,978 --> 00:13:34,397
HIS HAIR NEVER BOTHERED ME
THAT MUCH.

365
00:13:34,439 --> 00:13:38,526
AND, YOU KNOW, IT WAS ALWAYS
MORE CRUNCHY THAN IT WAS GREASY.

366
00:13:38,568 --> 00:13:40,570
OKAY.

367
00:13:40,612 --> 00:13:43,156
THIS'LL BE HARDER
THAN I THOUGHT.

368
00:13:43,197 --> 00:13:45,950
UM, LET'S TRY SOME
AVERSION THERAPY.

369
00:13:45,992 --> 00:13:46,951
OKAY.
OKAY?

370
00:13:46,993 --> 00:13:48,244
SO LOOK AT THE PICTURE.

371
00:13:48,286 --> 00:13:49,370
OKAY.
ALL RIGHT.

372
00:13:49,412 --> 00:13:51,205
AND, UM...

373
00:13:52,791 --> 00:13:53,958
OW!

374
00:13:57,128 --> 00:13:59,464
OKAY. HOW DO YOU FEEL NOW?

375
00:13:59,506 --> 00:14:01,716
WELL, I LIKE YOU LESS.

376
00:14:14,937 --> 00:14:15,938
HEY.

377
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:18,065
HEY.

378
00:14:21,235 --> 00:14:22,362
OH. SORRY.

379
00:14:22,403 --> 00:14:23,946
YOU KNOW WHAT?

380
00:14:23,988 --> 00:14:24,947
I'M SORRY.

381
00:14:24,989 --> 00:14:26,407
I REALLY SHOULDN'T
HAVE SAID

382
00:14:26,449 --> 00:14:27,950
THAT YOU WERE
EMBARRASSING ME.

383
00:14:27,992 --> 00:14:29,452
THAT REALLY
WASN'T COOL.

384
00:14:29,494 --> 00:14:31,705
IF IT MAKES YOU
FEEL ANY BETTER

385
00:14:31,746 --> 00:14:33,748
I'VE HAD A
REALLY LOUSY DAY.

386
00:14:33,790 --> 00:14:36,292
ME, TOO.

387
00:14:36,334 --> 00:14:37,377
YEAH?

388
00:14:37,418 --> 00:14:38,169
NO!

389
00:14:39,671 --> 00:14:41,631
I HAD THE BEST DAY EVER.

390
00:14:42,923 --> 00:14:45,635
DUDE, CHECK THIS OUT.

391
00:14:45,677 --> 00:14:47,261
HEY!

392
00:14:47,303 --> 00:14:48,179
SHH, SHH.

393
00:14:49,806 --> 00:14:52,809
Say hi to my friend
and tell him you like my hat.

394
00:14:52,851 --> 00:14:54,352
So what's your
friend's name?

395
00:14:54,394 --> 00:14:55,353
Chandler.

396
00:14:55,395 --> 00:14:56,646
Okay. So, hi, Chandler.

397
00:14:56,688 --> 00:14:58,606
THAT... THAT WAS...

398
00:14:58,648 --> 00:15:01,108
THAT'S FERGIE, BABY!

399
00:15:02,527 --> 00:15:05,321
Joey says you don't
really like his hat

400
00:15:05,363 --> 00:15:07,782
but I think it's
kind of dashing.

401
00:15:07,824 --> 00:15:09,409
WHEN DID YOU...? HOW...?

402
00:15:09,450 --> 00:15:12,328
I WAS TRYING TO FIGURE OUT
HOW TO GET TO BUCKINGHAM PALACE

403
00:15:12,370 --> 00:15:13,663
SO I'M IN MY MAP, AND...

404
00:15:13,705 --> 00:15:14,831
HEY.

405
00:15:14,873 --> 00:15:16,708
HEY.

406
00:15:16,750 --> 00:15:20,378
I UNDERSTAND YOU HAD
A LITTLE TALK WITH EMILY.

407
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:22,296
YES, I DID.

408
00:15:22,338 --> 00:15:25,800
AND YOU ARE WELCOME.

409
00:15:25,842 --> 00:15:27,301
AM I?

410
00:15:29,053 --> 00:15:31,723
AND WAS IT YOUR IDEA
TO POSTPONE THE WEDDING?

411
00:15:31,765 --> 00:15:34,517
UM...

412
00:15:34,559 --> 00:15:36,436
I'M GOING TO GO
TO THE BATHROOM.

413
00:15:36,477 --> 00:15:37,437
WAIT UP.

414
00:15:37,478 --> 00:15:39,856
HEY, HEY.

415
00:15:39,898 --> 00:15:41,608
SINCE YOU'RE
THE FIX-IT LADY

416
00:15:41,649 --> 00:15:42,734
HERE'S A PICKLE.

417
00:15:42,776 --> 00:15:44,944
WHAT DO YOU DO
WHEN THE BRIDE SAYS

418
00:15:44,985 --> 00:15:47,864
SHE DOESN'T WANT TO HAVE
THE WEDDING AT ALL?

419
00:15:47,906 --> 00:15:48,948
SHE SAID THAT?

420
00:15:48,989 --> 00:15:49,949
YEAH.

421
00:15:49,990 --> 00:15:50,949
WHY?

422
00:15:50,991 --> 00:15:52,535
I DON'T KNOW.

423
00:15:52,577 --> 00:15:54,036
I TOLD HER IT WAS STUPID

424
00:15:54,078 --> 00:15:56,623
TO PUT OFF THE WEDDING
JUST BECAUSE THE HALL WAS GONE

425
00:15:56,664 --> 00:15:57,749
AND SHE LIKE FLIPPED OUT.

426
00:15:57,791 --> 00:15:58,792
OH, MY GOD.

427
00:15:58,833 --> 00:16:01,335
YOU'RE EVEN DUMBER
THAN I AM.

428
00:16:01,377 --> 00:16:02,837
EXCUSE ME?

429
00:16:02,879 --> 00:16:06,716
ROSS, HOW LONG HAVE YOU
BEEN PLANNING THIS WEDDING?

430
00:16:06,758 --> 00:16:08,885
I DON'T KNOW. A MONTH.

431
00:16:08,927 --> 00:16:11,805
EMILY HAS PROBABLY
BEEN PLANNING IT
SINCE SHE WAS FIVE--

432
00:16:11,846 --> 00:16:14,223
EVER SINCE THE FIRST TIME
SHE TOOK A PILLOWCASE

433
00:16:14,265 --> 00:16:16,183
AND HUNG IT OFF
THE BACK OF HER HEAD.

434
00:16:17,852 --> 00:16:19,479
THAT'S WHAT WE DID.

435
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:22,523
WE DREAMED ABOUT
THE PERFECT WEDDING...

436
00:16:22,565 --> 00:16:25,067
AND THE PERFECT PLACE...

437
00:16:25,109 --> 00:16:28,780
WITH THE PERFECT
FOUR-TIERED
WEDDING CAKE...

438
00:16:28,822 --> 00:16:32,283
WITH THE LITTLE
PEOPLE ON TOP.

439
00:16:41,334 --> 00:16:44,170
BUT THE MOST
IMPORTANT PART

440
00:16:44,211 --> 00:16:46,506
IS THAT WE HAD
THE PERFECT GUY

441
00:16:46,547 --> 00:16:49,007
WHO UNDERSTOOD
JUST HOW IMPORTANT

442
00:16:49,049 --> 00:16:51,511
ALL THAT OTHER STUFF WAS.

443
00:16:53,471 --> 00:16:54,597
I HAD NO IDEA.

444
00:16:54,639 --> 00:16:56,474
THAT PILLOWCASE THING?

445
00:16:56,516 --> 00:17:00,770
I THOUGHT YOU GUYS
WERE JUST DOING THE FLYING NUN.

446
00:17:02,647 --> 00:17:04,899
SOMETIMES WE WERE.

447
00:17:04,941 --> 00:17:07,527
COME ON.

448
00:17:07,568 --> 00:17:10,530
YOU'RE GOING TO HELP ME
FIGURE OUT WHAT TO DO, OKAY?

449
00:17:10,571 --> 00:17:11,531
OKAY.

450
00:17:11,572 --> 00:17:12,573
COME ON.

451
00:17:16,076 --> 00:17:18,579
WELL, PRETTY
INTENSE, HUH?

452
00:17:18,621 --> 00:17:20,080
YEAH.

453
00:17:20,122 --> 00:17:22,750
HEY, I HOPE ROSS DIDN'T
THINK WE JUST WENT IN THERE

454
00:17:22,792 --> 00:17:25,127
BECAUSE WE WERE
UNCOMFORTABLE
BEING OUT HERE.

455
00:17:30,675 --> 00:17:32,969
I HOPE HE DID.

456
00:17:36,472 --> 00:17:39,308
( phone ringing )

457
00:17:40,351 --> 00:17:41,435
HELLO.

458
00:17:41,477 --> 00:17:43,062
HEY, PHEEBS. IT'S JOEY.

459
00:17:43,103 --> 00:17:44,146
HEY, JOEY. HEY, OH.

460
00:17:44,188 --> 00:17:45,523
OH, I JUST SAW SOMEONE

461
00:17:45,565 --> 00:17:47,775
THAT LOOKS JUST LIKE YOU
ON THE SUBWAY

462
00:17:47,817 --> 00:17:49,986
AND I WAS GOING TO GO OVER
AND SAY HI

463
00:17:50,028 --> 00:17:53,280
BUT THEN I FIGURED, HE
DOESN'T CARE HE LOOKS LIKE YOU.

464
00:17:53,322 --> 00:17:55,658
THAT JUST COST ME FOUR BUCKS.

465
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:57,785
BUT, LISTEN, I JUST CALLED

466
00:17:57,827 --> 00:18:01,288
TO SEE HOW THE CHICK
AND THE DUCK ARE DOING.

467
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:04,000
THEY'RE HAVING A GREAT TIME
WITH THEIR AUNT PHOEBE.

468
00:18:04,042 --> 00:18:05,001
AUNT RACHEL

469
00:18:05,043 --> 00:18:06,794
HASN'T BEEN
HELPFUL AT ALL.

470
00:18:06,836 --> 00:18:08,295
SO DO YOU MISS ME?

471
00:18:08,337 --> 00:18:11,298
KIND OF, BUT I'VE JUST
BEEN HAVING WAY TOO MUCH FUN.

472
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:12,967
OH, SO YOU'RE NOT HOMESICK YET?

473
00:18:13,009 --> 00:18:16,637
NO. I DON'T THINK SO.

474
00:18:16,679 --> 00:18:19,139
ALL RIGHT, WELL,
THE SEVEN OF US MISS YOU.

475
00:18:22,351 --> 00:18:23,519
WHO'S SEVEN?

476
00:18:23,561 --> 00:18:25,063
WELL, YOU KNOW,
ME, RACHEL

477
00:18:25,104 --> 00:18:26,606
THE BIRDS, THE BABIES.

478
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:29,984
AW, THE BABIES MISS ME?

479
00:18:30,026 --> 00:18:31,903
( knocking )
PIZZA GUY'S HERE.

480
00:18:31,945 --> 00:18:34,238
YOU ORDERED PIZZA WITHOUT ME?

481
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:36,824
YEAH, BUT, YOU KNOW,
WE WERE THINKING ABOUT YOU.

482
00:18:36,866 --> 00:18:38,868
YOU KNOW, WE ORDERED
THE JOEY SPECIAL.

483
00:18:38,910 --> 00:18:40,745
TWO PIZZAS?

484
00:18:40,787 --> 00:18:41,746
( door closing )

485
00:18:41,788 --> 00:18:42,747
YEP.

486
00:18:42,789 --> 00:18:44,123
OKAY, GOT TO GO.

487
00:18:44,164 --> 00:18:45,124
TALK TO YOU LATER.

488
00:18:45,165 --> 00:18:47,835
WAIT. WHERE DID YOU GET IT FROM?

489
00:18:53,091 --> 00:18:56,385
♪ ...Where everybody
knows your name ♪

490
00:18:56,427 --> 00:18:58,137
( bouncy tune )

491
00:18:58,178 --> 00:19:02,224
♪ And they're
always glad you came ♪

492
00:19:02,266 --> 00:19:05,519
♪ You want to be
where you can see ♪

493
00:19:05,561 --> 00:19:07,855
♪ Troubles are all the same ♪

494
00:19:07,897 --> 00:19:12,860
♪ You want to be where
everybody knows your name. ♪

495
00:19:15,529 --> 00:19:16,948
MONICA, WHY HAVE YOU

496
00:19:16,990 --> 00:19:19,408
BROUGHT ME HERE
OF ALL PLACES?

497
00:19:19,450 --> 00:19:20,493
YOU'LL SEE.

498
00:19:20,534 --> 00:19:22,954
I TELL YOU, THIS WEDDING

499
00:19:22,996 --> 00:19:25,164
IS NOT GOING TO HAPPEN.

500
00:19:25,205 --> 00:19:27,166
OH, GOD.

501
00:19:27,207 --> 00:19:30,670
OKAY, BUT IMAGINE
A LOT MORE LIGHTS, OKAY?

502
00:19:30,711 --> 00:19:34,214
AND... AND, YOU KNOW,
FEWER BRICKS, AND...

503
00:19:34,256 --> 00:19:36,383
AND FLOWERS AND CANDLES.

504
00:19:36,425 --> 00:19:38,636
AND THE MUSICIANS--
THEY CAN GO OVER HERE

505
00:19:38,678 --> 00:19:40,805
AND THE CHAIRS--
THEY CAN FACE THIS WAY

506
00:19:40,847 --> 00:19:41,764
AND...

507
00:19:41,806 --> 00:19:43,057
YOU GO.

508
00:19:43,099 --> 00:19:45,685
BUT... BUT IF YOU
DON'T LOVE THIS

509
00:19:45,726 --> 00:19:49,396
THEN WE'LL DO IT
ANY OTHER PLACE, ANY OTHER TIME.

510
00:19:49,438 --> 00:19:52,232
REALLY, IT'S FINE.
WHATEVER YOU WANT.

511
00:19:52,274 --> 00:19:55,444
IT'S PERFECT.

512
00:19:55,486 --> 00:19:58,114
AND, I DON'T KNOW, IF
IT STARTS TO RAIN...

513
00:19:58,156 --> 00:19:59,907
WELL, THEN WE'LL GET WET.

514
00:20:03,452 --> 00:20:05,579
OH...

515
00:20:05,621 --> 00:20:07,707
I DON'T EVEN HAVE A DATE.

516
00:20:09,834 --> 00:20:10,793
Rachel:
PHEEBS?

517
00:20:10,835 --> 00:20:11,961
YEAH?

518
00:20:12,003 --> 00:20:14,088
YOU REMEMBER WHERE
THE DUCK FOOD IS?

519
00:20:14,130 --> 00:20:17,008
IT'S IN THE GUYS' APARTMENT
UNDER THE SINK. WHY?

520
00:20:17,050 --> 00:20:19,217
'CAUSE I'M GOING TO LONDON.

521
00:20:19,259 --> 00:20:20,178
WHAT?!

522
00:20:20,219 --> 00:20:21,345
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

523
00:20:21,387 --> 00:20:23,764
I HAVE TO TELL ROSS
THAT I LOVE HIM.

524
00:20:23,806 --> 00:20:25,432
NOW, HONEY, YOU TAKE CARE.

525
00:20:25,474 --> 00:20:28,268
YOU DON'T HAVE THOSE BABIES
TILL I GET BACK.

526
00:20:28,310 --> 00:20:29,436
RACHEL, YOU CAN'T GO.

527
00:20:29,478 --> 00:20:30,437
ROSS LOVES EMILY.

528
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:31,731
I KNOW. I KNOW HE DOES

529
00:20:31,772 --> 00:20:33,566
BUT I HAVE TO TELL HIM
HOW I FEEL.

530
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:35,860
HE DESERVES TO HAVE
ALL OF THE INFORMATION

531
00:20:35,902 --> 00:20:38,154
AND THEN HE CAN MAKE
AN INFORMED DECISION.

532
00:20:38,196 --> 00:20:39,822
THAT'S NOT WHY YOU'RE GOING.

533
00:20:39,864 --> 00:20:42,616
YOU'RE GOING BECAUSE YOU HOPE
HE'S GOING TO SAY

534
00:20:42,658 --> 00:20:44,451
"YEAH, I LOVE YOU, TOO, RACH.

535
00:20:44,493 --> 00:20:46,579
FORGET ABOUT THAT
BRITISH CHIPPY."

536
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:47,997
DO YOU THINK HE WILL?

537
00:20:48,039 --> 00:20:51,918
NO, BECAUSE HE'S IN LOVE
WITH THE BRITISH CHIPPY.

538
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:53,961
RACHEL, IF YOU GO

539
00:20:54,003 --> 00:20:56,130
YOU'RE JUST GOING
TO MESS WITH HIS HEAD

540
00:20:56,172 --> 00:20:57,339
AND RUIN HIS WEDDING.

541
00:20:57,381 --> 00:20:58,799
YOU KNOW, IT'S TOO LATE.

542
00:20:58,841 --> 00:21:00,259
YOU MISSED YOUR CHANCE.

543
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:01,343
I'M SORRY.

544
00:21:01,385 --> 00:21:03,221
I KNOW THIS MUST
BE REALLY HARD.

545
00:21:03,262 --> 00:21:06,891
IT'S OVER.

546
00:21:09,852 --> 00:21:11,187
YOU KNOW WHAT? NO.

547
00:21:11,229 --> 00:21:13,647
IT'S NOT OVER
UNTIL SOMEONE SAYS, "I DO."

548
00:21:13,689 --> 00:21:14,815
I DO.

549
00:21:14,857 --> 00:21:16,067
I DO. I DO.

550
00:21:16,109 --> 00:21:17,359
I DO! I DO!

551
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:21,572
( groans )

552
00:21:21,614 --> 00:21:24,533
YEAH, LIKE I CAN
REALLY CHASE YOU.

553
00:21:24,575 --> 00:21:26,619
I'M CARRYING A LITTER.

